hadiths[297]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1511","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good, or remain silent” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. This is clear that he should not speak unless the speech is good, and it (the speech) is the one whose benefit has become clear, and if he doubts whether the benefit will appear, then he should not speak."
"1512","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which Muslims are better? He said: “The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1513","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever guarantees for me what is between his two jaws and what is between his feet, I guarantee him Paradise” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1514","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “When a servant speaks a word that he does not reflect upon (i.e., does not consider if it is good or evil), he will be sent down to Hell farther than what is between the East and the West” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Meaning: It becomes clear, he ponders whether it is good or not."
"1515","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “A servant may speak a word out of the pleasure of Allah Almighty that he does not care about, for which Allah will raise him in degrees, and if a servant speaks a word out of the displeasure of Allah Almighty, without paying attention to it, he will fall into Hell with it.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1516","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman Bilal bin al-Harith al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man may speak a word that pleases Allah Almighty and does not think that it will reach what it has reached. Allah will record His pleasure for him with it until the day he meets him, and a man may speak a word that incurs Allah’s displeasure, which he did not think would reach what it has reached. Allah will record his displeasure with it until the day he meets him.” It was narrated by Malik in Al-Muwatta’ and Al-Tirmidhi and he said. A good and authentic hadith."
"1517","And on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, tell me something that I will adhere to. He said: “Say, ‘My Lord is Allah,’ and then be upright.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do I fear that you fear for me?” So he took hold of his own tongue, then said: “This.” Al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said it was a good and authentic hadith."
"1518","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not talk a lot without mentioning Allah, for too much talk without mentioning Allah Almighty hardens the heart! And indeed the hardest heart is the farthest of people from Allah.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1519","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “And whoever Allah protects from the evil between his two jaws and the evil between his two feet will enter Paradise.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1520","On the authority of Uqba bin Amer, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is salvation? He said: “Hold your tongue, and let your home suffice for you (i.e., remain at home, avoid unnecessary outings), and cry over your sin” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1521","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “When the son of Adam wakes up, all the limbs will disbelieve the tongue, saying: Fear Allah regarding us, for we are only in you: if you are upright, we will be upright, and if you are crooked, we will be crooked.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1522","And on the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah: Tell me about a deed that will bring me into Paradise and keep me away from Hell? He said: “You have asked about a great matter, and it is easy for whomever Allah Almighty makes it easy for him: You worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, pay zakat, fast Ramadan, and perform the Hajj to the House if you are able to do so. Then he said: Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and a man’s prayer in the middle of the night.” Then he recited: “Their sides shall turn away from their beds” until he reached: “They shall work” [Al-Sajdah: 16-17]. Then he said: “Shall I not inform you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and its climax? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The head of the matter is Islam, its pillar is prayer, and the top of its top is jihad. Then he said: Shall I not tell you the meaning of all of that? May your mother be bereft of you! Is there anything that causes people to be thrown into Hell on their faces except the harvest of their tongues? [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1523","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do you know what backbiting is?” They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “Mentioning your brother in a way that he dislikes.” It was said: Have you seen if there is in my brother what I say? He said: “If he has what you say, then you have backbited him, and if he does not have what you say, then you have slandered him.” [Muslim]."
"1524","On the authority of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said in his sermon on the Day of Sacrifice in Mina during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Your blood, your property, and your honor are as sacred to you as this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this country of yours. Have you not conveyed the message?” (Agreed upon)."
"1525","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: She said: I said to the Prophet (ﷺ) “Sufiya is such-and-such.” Some of the narrators said: It means short, so he said: “You said a word that if it were mixed with sea water, it would mix with it!” She said: And I told him about a person, and he said: “I do not like that I should mention a person while I have such-and-such.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud) And Al-Tirmidhi said it is a good and authentic hadith.] And the meaning of: “I mixed it” with it in a mixture that changes its taste or smell due to the intensity of its stench and ugliness, and this hadith is one of the most eloquent of the signs of backbiting. Allah Almighty said: {And he does not speak out of inclination; it is only a revelation revealed}."
"1526","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When he ascended with me, I passed by a people who had nails made of copper scratching their faces and chests, and I said: Who are these, O Gabriel? He said: These are the ones who eat people’s flesh and cut their honor!” [Narrated by Abu Dawud.]"
"1527","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Everything of a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his blood, his honor, and his property.” [Muslim]."
"1528","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who defends the honour of his (Muslim) brother"","" Allah will secure his face against the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.\"" [At-Tirmidhi] .""
"1529","And on the authority of Itban bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, in his long and famous hadith that was presented in the chapter on hope, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) stood up to pray and said: “Where is Malik ibn al-Dakhsham?” A man said: That is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Do not say that, do you not see that he said: There is no god but Allah, intending by that the face of Allah! “The face of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. “And itban” with the well-known kasra of the ‘ayn, and it is said to include it, and after it a double ta’ from above, then a unified ba. And “Al-Dakhsham” with the addition of the dal and the sukka of the kha and the tampering of the two lexical shin."
"1530","The Prophet (ﷺ) was sitting among the people in Tabuk. He (ﷺ) said, What happened to Ka'b bin Malik?\"" A person from the tribe of Banu Salamah said: \""O Messenger of Allah! his cloak has held him back"","" and he is turning to his sides [in arrogance]"","" and he was thus detained.\"" Mu'adh bin Jabal (May Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Woe be upon you! You have passed indecent remarks. O Messenger of Allah! by Allah"","" we know nothing about him but good.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained silent. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1531","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that a man asked permission to go before the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: “Grant him permission, what an evil brother of the clan he is” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Al-Bukhari used it as evidence in the permissibility of the backbiting of corrupt people and people of suspicion."
"1532","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, I do not think that so-and-so understands anything of our Faith.\"" [Al-Bukhari] Al-Bukhari said: Al- Laith bin Sa'd"","" who is one of the narrators of this Hadith"","" said: The two men mentioned by the Prophet (ﷺ) in this Hadith were hypocrites (i.e."","" they revealed Faith and concealed disbelief).""
"1533","I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said to him: Muawiyah and Abul-Jahm sent me a proposal of marriage.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""Muawiyah is destitute and he has no property"","" and as for Abul-Jahm"","" he does not put the stick off his shoulder.\"" [Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1534","On the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey during which the people were distressed. Abdullah bin Ubayy said: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse. He said: If we return to Medina, the more honorable will expel from it the meaner. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him of that. He sent for Abdullah bin Ubayy, and he made an effort to swear his oath: what he did. They said: Zaid has lied against the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and what they said became distressing to me until Allah Almighty revealed my belief {When the hypocrites come to you} Then the Prophet (ﷺ) called them to ask forgiveness for them, so they bowed their heads. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1535","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Hind, Abu Sufyan’s wife, said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and he does not give me what is sufficient for me and my child except what I took from him, and he does not know? He said: “Take what is sufficient for you and your child, according to what is reasonable” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1536","On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A slanderer will not enter Paradise” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1537","And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by two graves and said: “They are being tormented, but they are not being tormented for a major matter! Indeed, it is a major one: As for one of them, he used to go about gossiping, and as for the other, he would not cover himself from his urine [Agreed upon, and this is the wording of one of Al-Bukhari’s narrations]. The scholars said: The meaning of “And they are not tormented for a reason.” “Kabir” means big according to their claim, and it was said: “Kabir” left it on them"
"1538","And on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not tell you what is a bite? It is gossip and gossip among people” [Muslim]. Al-'Adhah: It is pronounced with the opening of the 'ayn (the first letter), the silencing of the ḍād (the second letter), and a final hā, on the pattern of 'wajh' (face). It is also narrated as 'al-'adhah' with the breaking of the 'ayn, the opening of the ḍād, on the pattern of 'iddah' (waiting period), and it means lying and slander. According to the first narration, 'al-'adhah' is a verbal noun (masdar); it is said: 'adhahahu 'adhā', meaning: he accused him of 'adhah (gossip/backbiting)."
"1539","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of my companions should inform me of anything about anyone, for I like to go out to you with a heart free of resentment towards you.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1540","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, People are like ores. Those who were excellent in the Days of Ignorance are excellent in Islam provided they acquire the knowledge and understanding of the religion. You will find the best people in it (Islam) those who had a deep hatred (for leadership). You will find the worst among the people a double-faced person who appears to some people with one face and to others with another face.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1541","And on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid that people said to his grandfather Abdullah bin Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both: We go to our sultans and say to them the opposite of what we say when we leave them. He said: We used to consider this hypocrisy during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Al-Bukhari]."
"1542","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise, and a man tells the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a friend, and lying leads to immorality, and immorality leads to Hell, and a man lies until he is recorded with Allah as a liar” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1543","And on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There are four qualities: whoever has one of them is a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of them has a characteristic of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when he is trusted, he betrays, when he speaks, he lies, when he makes a covenant, he is treacherous, and when he quarrels, he is obscene.” (Agreed upon) This has been explained previously with a hadith. Abu Hurairah said something similar in the chapter on fulfilling a covenant."
"1544","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who narrates a dream which he has not seen will be put to trouble to join into a knot two barley seeds which he will not be able to do; and he who seeks to listen to the talk of a people (secretly) will have molten lead poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection; and he who makes a picture (of people or other creatures with a soul"","" such as animals and insects) will be (severely punished)"","" and he will be asked to infuse spirit therein"","" which he will not be able to do.\"" [Al-Bukhari] .""
"1545","The Prophet (ﷺ) as saying: The worst of lies is to pretend to have seen something which he has not seen.\"" [Al- Bukhari] .""
"1546","On the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would often say to his companions: [Has any of you seen a vision?] and he would narrate to him whomever Allah wished for him to narrate, and that he said to us one morning: ((Two came to me tonight, and they said to me: Go, and I set off with them, and we came to a man. He was lying down, and behold, another person was standing on top of him with a rock, and behold, he was falling with the rock on his head, and his head was stabbed, and the stone was threatening him here, so he followed the stone and took it, and did not return to it until his head was healthy as it was, then he would return to him, and do to him the same as he did the first time! On a man lying on his back, and another man was standing over him with an iron hook, and then he approached one side of his face and split his cheek to the back of his face, his nostril to the back of his head, and his eye to the back of his head. Then he turned to the other side and did to him the same as he did to the first side. He did not finish that side until that side became healthy as it was, then he returned to it and did the same as he did the first time. He said: I said: Glory be to Allah? What are these two? He said: They said to me: “Go, go.” So we went, and we came to something like an oven. I think he said: “So there was commotion and voices in it. So we looked into it, and there were naked men and women in it. And when flames came to them from below them, when that flame came to them, they lit up. I said: Who are these? They said to me: “Go, go.” So we set off and came to a river. I thought it was a river. He says: “Red like blood, and behold, in the river there is a man swimming, and behold, on the bank of the river there is a man who has collected many stones with him, and behold, that swimmer is cursing what he is swimming, then the one who has collected stones with him comes, and his mouth opens for him, and he throws him a stone, and he goes swimming, and then returns to him. Whenever he returns to him, he opens his mouth for him, and he throws a stone at him. I said to them: What are these? Go, so we set off, and we came upon a man who ugly appearance, or as I hate seeing a man of sight, and lo and behold, he had a fire that he was stoking and running around. I said to them: What is this? He said to me: Go, go, so we set off and came to a dark meadow in which there was all the light of spring, and behold, between my backs of the meadow was a tall man whose head I could hardly see as tall as the sky. And when the man was among the boys I had ever seen, I said: What is this? And what are these? They said to me: Go, go, so we set off, and we came to a great city. I have never seen a city greater than it, nor better! They said to me: Ascend for me: ascend in it. So we ascended there to a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver. We came to the gate of the city and asked for it to be opened. It was opened for us, so we entered it, and men met us. Half of their creation is like the best of what you are seeing! And half of them is like the ugliest of what you are seeing! They said to them: Go and fall into that river, and behold, it was an flowing river flowing as if its pure water was white, so they went and fell into it. Then they returned to us, that evil had gone from them, and they became in the best form. He said: They said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and this is your home, so my vision cleared. They went up, and suddenly it was short like a white cloud. They said to me: This is your house? I said to them: May Allah bless you both, so let me go in. They said: Now no, and you are inside it. I said to them: Since tonight I have seen a wonder? So what is this that I have seen? They said to me: But we will tell you: As for the first man whom I came to stabbing his head with a stone, he is the man who takes the Qur’an and rejects it. And he sleeps and misses the obligatory prayer. As for the man whom you came to, his mouth to the back of his mouth, his nostril to the back of his mouth, and his eye to the back of his mouth, then he is the man who goes out of his house in the morning and tells lies that reach the horizons. As for the naked men and women who are like building an oven, they are adulterers and adulterers. As for the man whom you came to who is swimming in the river and throwing stones, he is a usurer. As for the man who is a mirror ball who is at the fire, stoking it and running around it, he is Malik. The keeper of Hell, and as for the tall man in the garden, he is Abraham, and as for the children around him, every child who was born died according to the fitrah.” And in Al-Barqani’s narration: “He was born according to the fitrah.” Some Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, and the children of the polytheists? Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “And the children of the polytheists, and as for the people of whom half of them were good and half of them were ugly, they are a people.” They mixed good deeds with bad deeds, Allah has overlooked them” [Al-Bukhari]. And in his narration: “Tonight I saw two men who came to me and took me out to a holy land.” Then he mentioned it and said: “So we went to a pit like an oven, the top of which is narrow and the bottom is wide; A fire burned beneath it, and when it rose, they rose until they were about to come out, and when it died down, they returned to it, and therein were naked men and women. And in it: “Until we came upon a river of blood,” and he did not doubt, “therein was a man standing in the middle of the river, and on the bank of the river was a man, with stones in front of him. The man who was in the river approached, and when he wanted to come out, the man threw a stone into his mouth, and he returned it to where it was, so he made every time he came Then he would go out and start throwing a stone at me, and he would return as he was.” And in it: “So they took me up the tree and took me into a house that I had never seen better than it, in which there were old men and young men.” And in it: “The one who I saw having his mouth split open is a liar. He tells a lie and it is carried from him until it reaches the horizons, and what I saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection.” And in it: “The one who I saw cutting his head off is a liar. So, a man was taught by Allah the Qur’an, but he slept on it at night and did not work on it during the day, so he will do it until the Day of Resurrection. The first house that he entered is the house of the common believers. As for this house, it is the house of the martyrs, and I am Gabriel, and this is Michael, so raise your head. So I raised my head, and behold, above me there was something like a cloud. They said: That is your house. I said: Let me enter my house. They said: You have a lifetime remaining that you have not completed, so if you complete it, I will come to your house. [Al-Bukhari]. His saying: “He makes his head thick” is with the triangular tha’ and the grammatical ghān, i.e. he makes it hard and splits it. His saying: “he makes it sag” meaning he rolls over, and “the klub” is with the opening of the kāf and the tightening of the lam. It is well-known for his saying: “fişrār” which means: he cuts it with two dictionary antonyms, i.e. they shouted. “Fifghar” is with the fa and ghān in the dictionary, that is, he opens it. His saying “the mirror” is with the opening of the meem, meaning: the sight. His saying: “he fills it” is with the fatḥah of the yā and the ḍāḍ of the neglected ha and the ḍān with the ḥā’ The neglected: which is the large tree. His saying: “the pure” is with the opening of the meem and the suffix of the neglected ha and with the lexicalized dād, which is: milk. His saying, “So my sight rose,” meaning: it rose. And “saada” is combined with the ḍād and the ʿā’, meaning: high. And “al-Rabbabah” is pronounced with the letter “Ra’” opened and with the unified “baa” repeated, which is: the cloud"
"1547","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “It is enough of a lie for a man to narrate everything he hears.” [Muslim]"
"1548","On the authority of Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever narrates a hadith from me that he believes is a lie, then he is one of the liars” [Muslim]."
"1549","A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: I have a co-wife. \""Is there any harm for me if I give her the false impression of getting something from my husband which he has not in fact given me?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""The one who creates a false impression of receiving what one has not been given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1550","On the authority of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Associating partners with Allah and being disobedient to one’s parents.” He was reclining and sat down, so he said: “And false speech!” He continued repeating it until We said: I wish he had been silent. Agreed upon"
"1551","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, He who swears an oath by a religion other than Islam"","" intentionally lying"","" is as he said. He who kills himself with something"","" will be tormented with it on the Day of Resurrection. A person is not bound to fulfill a vow about something which he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like murdering him.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1552","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A friend should not be a curser” [Muslim]."
"1553","On the authority of Abu Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Those who curse will not be intercessors, nor will they be martyrs on the Day of Resurrection” [Muslim]."
"1554","On the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not curse with the curse of Allah, nor with His anger, nor with fire.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1555","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A believer is not one who slanders, curses, is obscene, or obscene.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1556","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, When a person curses somebody or something"","" the curse goes up to heaven and the gates of heaven get closed. Then it comes down to the earth and its gates get closed. Then it turns right and left"","" and if it does not find an entrance to go anywhere"","" it returns to the person or thing that was cursed; if he or it deserves to be cursed; otherwise it returns to the person who uttered it.\"" [Abu Dawud] .""
"1557","We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey and there was a woman from the Ansar riding a she-camel. She became annoyed and invoked curse upon it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard it and said, Off load the she- camel and set it free because it has been cursed.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1558","On the authority of Abu Barza Nadhla bin Ubaid Al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, he said while she was riding a camel carrying some of the people’s belongings, when she saw the Prophet (ﷺ) and the mountain harassing them, she said: Move (O camel), O Allah, curse her. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Do not accompany us with a camel upon which there is a curse” [Muslim]. His statement: It is permissible to open the neglected haa, and place the lam in place, which is a word to rebuke camels. Know that the meaning of this hadith may be ambiguous, and there is no problem with it. Rather, what is meant is the prohibition on accompanying that camel with them, and it does not contain a prohibition on selling it, slaughtering it, or riding it in other than the company of the Prophet (ﷺ). Rather, all of that and other actions are permissible, and there is no prohibition from it except from accompanying him (ﷺ) because all of these actions were permissible, so some of them were prohibited, so the rest remained as it was. And Allah knows best"
"1559","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Cursing a Muslim is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1560","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, When any Muslim accuses another Muslim of sin or of disbelief"","" the reproach rebounds upon the one who utters it"","" if the other person is not deserving of it.\"" [Al- Bukhari] .""
"1561","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, When two persons indulge in abusing each other"","" the beginner will be the sinner so long as the oppressed does not transgress the limits.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1562","On his authority, he said: A man who had drunk was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ). He said: “Strike him.” Abu Hurairah said: Among us is the one who strikes with his hand, the one who strikes with his shoe, and the one who strikes with his garment. When he left, some of the people said: May Allah disgrace you. He said: “Do not say this, do not help Satan against him.” [Al-Bukhari].."
"1563","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever accuses his slave of adultery, the punishment will be imposed on him on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1564","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not curse the dead, for they have returned to what they brought forward.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1565","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and an immigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1566","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, He who desires to be rescued from the fire of Hell and to enter Jannah"","" should die in a state of complete belief in Allah and the Last Day"","" and should do unto others what he wishes to be done unto him.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1567","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Do not hate each other, do not envy one another, do not separate one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1568","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, The gates of Jannah are opened on Mondays and Thursdays"","" and then every slave (of Allah) is granted forgiveness if he does not associate anything with Allah in worship. But the person in whose heart there is rancour against his (Muslim) brother"","" they will not be pardoned and with regard to them it will be said twice: 'Hold both of them until they are reconciled with each other.\""' [Muslim] .""
"1569","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Beware of envy, for envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood, or he said: grass.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1570","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not snoop secretly, do not spy, do not compete, do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers, as He commanded you. A Muslim is a brother to a Muslim. Do not oppress him, do not let him down, or despise him. Piety is here. And he points to his chest, “It is enough evil for a person to despise his Muslim brother. Everything that is sacred to a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his blood, his honor, and his property. Allah does not look at your bodies, nor at your images, but looks at your hearts and your deeds.” And in a narration: “Do not envy, and do not hate each other, and do not spy, and do not pry into others' affairs, and do not quarrel, and be servants of Allah.” “Brothers.” And in a narration: “Do not cut off relations with one another, do not turn away from one another, do not hate one another, and do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers.” And in a narration: “Do not boycott one another, and do not undercut one another in trade.” [All of these narrations were narrated by Muslim, and most of them were narrated by Al-Bukhari]."
"1571","On the authority of Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “If you follow the faults of the Muslims, you will corrupt them, or you will almost corrupt them.” An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with an authentic chain of transmission."
"1572","And on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man was brought and it was said to him, “This is so-and-so whose beard is dripping with wine,” so he said: “We have forbidden spying, but if something appears to us, we will take it.” A good and authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with a chain of transmission according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"1573","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1574","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is enough evil for a person to despise a Muslim.” [Narrated by Muslim, and it was mentioned earlier in full]."
"1575","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The haughty"","" even with pride equal to a mustard seed in his heart"","" will not enter Jannah.\"" A man enquired: \""What about that a person likes fine dress and fine shoes?\"" He said: \""Allah is Beautiful and likes beauty. Pride amounts to disclaiming truth out of self- esteem"","" and despising people .\"" [Muslim] .""
"1576","On the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man said: By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so, so Allah Almighty said: Who is it that tells me that I should not forgive so-and-so! For I have forgiven him, and I have thwarted your work” [Muslim]."
"1577","On the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not show gloating to your brother, for Allah will have mercy on him and test you.” [Al-Tirmidhi] And in the chapter is the previous hadith of Abu Hurairah in the chapter on spying: “Everything belonging to a Muslim is forbidden to another Muslim.” The hadith."
"1578","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Two matters are signs of disbelief on the part of those who indulge in them: Defaming and speaking evil of a person's lineage"","" and wailing over the dead.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1579","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever bears weapons against us is not of us, and whoever deceives us is not of us” [Muslim]. And in his narration, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a heap of food, put his hand into it, and his fingers got wet, so he said: “What is this, O owner of the food?” It was affected by rain from the sky, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Why didn’t you put it above the food so that people could see it? Whoever deceives us is not one of us.”"
"1580","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not engage in deceptive bidding (i.e. do not raise the price of an item for sale without intending to buy it)” (Agreed upon)."
"1581","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade Najsh (shill bidding in sales), [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1582","And on his authority, he said: A man mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he was deceived in sales, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Who did you sell to? So say: 'No deception.'” (Agreed upon))."
"1583","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever entices away or corrupts a man’s wife, or his slave, is not one of us.”"
"1584","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are four things: whoever has all of them is a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of them has a characteristic of hypocrisy until he abandons it: If he is trusted, he betrays his trust, when he speaks, he lies, if he makes a covenant, he is treacherous, and if he quarrels, he is unjust” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1585","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, For every one who breaks his covenant"","" there will be a (huge) flag on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: 'This flag proclaims a breach of covenant by so-and-so.\""' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1586","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Every one who breaks a covenant will have a flag by his buttocks on the Day of Resurrection. It will be raised higher according to the nature of his breach. Behold"","" there will be no greater a sin with respect to breaking the covenant than that of a ruler who breaks his covenant with the Muslim masses.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1587","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah"","" the Exalted"","" says: 'I will contend on the Day of Resurrection against three (types of) people: One who makes a covenant in My Name and then breaks it; one who sells a free man as a slave and devours his price; and one who hires a workman and having taken full work from him"","" does not pay him his wages.\""' [Al- Bukhari] .""
"1588","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There are three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them, nor will He purify them, and they will have a painful punishment.” He said: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited it three times. Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who drags his lower garment (izar) out of pride, the one who reminds others of his favors, and the one who sells his goods by swearing a false oath. And in another narration: 'The one who drags his izar' means: he lets his garment hang below the ankles out of vanity."
"1589","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Verily"","" Allah has revealed to me that you should adopt humility. So that no one may wrong another and no one may be disdainful and haughty towards another.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1590","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a man says: The people are destroyed, then he has destroyed them” [Muslim]. The famous narration: He destroyed them by raising the kaf, and it was narrated by putting it in the accusative case, and this is forbidden, and as for the one who said that, he is conceited and proud of himself, And being belittling people and being arrogant towards them, this is forbidden. As for whoever says it because he sees in people of deficiency in the matter of their religion, and says it out of sadness for them and for the religion, there is nothing wrong with it. This is how the scholars interpreted it and explained it in detail, and whoever said it among the eminent imams: Malik bin Anas, Al-Khattabi, Al-Humaidi and others, and I explained it in the book Al-Adhkar."
"1591","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Do not desert (stop talking to) one another"","" do not turn away from one another"","" do not nurse hatred towards one another"","" do not be jealous of one another"","" and become as fellow brothers and slaves of Allah. It is not lawful for a Muslim to stop talking to his brother (Muslim) for more than three days.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]""
"1592","On the authority of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a Muslim to desert his brother for more than three nights: they meet, and this one turns away and the other turns away, and the best of them is the one who begins with peace” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1593","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday, so Allah forgives every person who does not associate anything with Allah, except a man who has a grudge between him and his brother, and he says: Leave these two until they are reconciled” [Muslim]."
"1594","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Satan has despaired of the worshipers in the Arabian Peninsula worshiping him, but he is harassing them” [Muslim]. Harassing: corruption, changing their hearts, and interrupting them."
"1595","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days, so whoever abandons more than three days and dies will enter Hell.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud with a chain of transmission according to Al-Bukhari’s conditions]."
"1596","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, Whosoever forsakes his brother for a year is like one who sheds his blood.\"" [Abu Dawud] .""
"1597","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a believer to abandon a believer for more than three days. If three times have passed by him, let him meet him and greet him. If he returns the greeting to him, they have shared in the reward, but if he does not respond to him, then he has committed sin, and the Muslim is excluded from the migration.” ([Abu Dawud] Abu Dawud said: If this abandonment is for the sake of Allah, then it is not included in this prohibition.)"
"1598","the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, In the presence of three people"","" two should not hold secret counsel"","" to the exclusion of the third.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] . In Abu Dawud"","" Abu Salih related: I asked Ibn 'Umar: \""What if there are four people.\"" He said"","" \""There is no harm in that.\"" Malik reported in Al-Muwatta that 'Abdullah bin Dinar related: Ibn 'Umar and I were together in Khalid bin 'Uqbah's house which was situated in the market place. A man came to consult Ibn 'Umar. None besides me was present. Ibn 'Umar called another man in and we became four and said to me and the man he had called: Move away a bit because I have heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying"","" \""The two people should not hold secret counsel together excluding the third.\""
"1599","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If there are three of you, then two of you should not talk to each other without the other until you mix with the people, because that makes him sad” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1600","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A woman was tortured because of a cat that she kept until it died, so she entered the Fire. She neither fed it nor gave it drink, since she had locked it up, nor did she let it eat from the vermin of the earth.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. They are: their vermin and insects."
"1601","On his authority, he passed by young men from Quraish who had set up birds and were shooting at them, and they had given the owner of the bird every miss from their arrows. When they saw Ibn Umar, they dispersed, and Ibn Umar said: Who did this? May Allah curse whoever did this. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed whoever uses something that has a spirit in it as an object. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. “The purpose” : By opening the dictionary gān and rā’, which is the goal and the thing at which one is aiming"
"1602","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade animals to be restrained/tied up for slaughter. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. It means: to be locked up for killing."
"1603","I was the seventh of seven [brothers] from Banu Muqarrin and we had only one slave-girl. When the youngest of us once happened to slap her (on the face) the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us to set her free. [Muslim] ."
"1604","I was beating my slave with a whip when I heard a voice behind me which said: Abu Mas'ud! Bear in mind...\"" I did not recognize the voice for the intense anger I was in. Abu Mas'ud added: As he came near me"","" I found that he was the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who was saying"","" \""Abu Mas'ud! Bear in mind that Allah has more dominance upon you than you have upon your slave.\"" Then I said: \""I will never beat any slave in future.\"" Another narration is: The whip dropped from my hand in awe of the Prophet (ﷺ). Still another narration is: I said: \""He is free for the sake of Allah.\"" He (ﷺ) said"","" \""If you had not done this"","" you would have been scorched by the Fire.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1605","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever hits his slave for an offense he did not commit, or slaps him, his expiation is to free him” [Muslim]."
"1606","On the authority of Hisham bin Hakim bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, he passed through the Levant upon people from the Nabataeans, who were standing in the sun, and oil was poured on their heads. He said: What is this? They are being tortured for the tax, and in one narration: They were imprisoned for the jizyah. Hisham said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Allah punishes those who torture people in this world.” So he entered upon the prince, informed him of the situation, and the prince ordered them to be released.” [Narrated by Muslim. “Nabataeans” are farmers from the Persians]."
"1607","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw an ass which had been branded on the face. He disapproved of it. Upon this Ibn 'Abbas (May Allah be pleased with them) said, By Allah"","" I shall not brand (the animal) but on a part at a distance from the face.\"" Ibn 'Abbas (May Allah be pleased with them) then commanded branding on the hips; he was the first person to brand the animals on hips. [Muslim] .""
"1608","On his authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a donkey that had been branded in the face, and he said: “May Allah curse the one who marked him.” [Muslim] Also in a narration by Muslim: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade striking in the face, and marking in the face))."
"1609","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us on an expedition, and he said: “If you find so-and-so and so-and-so,” referring to two men from Quraish whom he named, “then burn them with fire.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said when we wanted to leave: “I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so, and no one will be punished with fire except By Allah, if you find them, kill them.” [Al-Bukhari]"
"1610","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey, and he set off for his needs, and we saw a red bird with two chicks, so we took her two chicks. The red bird came and started fluttering her wings in distress. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) came and said: “Who made this woman sad with her child? Return her child to her.” And he saw an ant village that we had burned, so he said: “Who burned this [ant colony]?” “This?” We said: “We.” He said: “No one should be punished with fire except the Lord of Fire.” His saying: “Qaryat an-Naml” means: “The place of an ant with an ant.”"
"1611","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Delaying payment by a rich person is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a judge regarding a full claim (debt), then he should follow the ruling” [Agreed upon. The meaning of “follow” ("
"1612","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The one who returns to his gift is like a dog who returns to his vomit.” (Agreed upon) ((And in a narration: “The example of one who returns to his charity is like a dog that vomits, then returns to its vomit and eats it.” And in a narration: “The one who returns to his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”)"
"1613","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I donated a horse for the cause of Allah, and the one who had it (the recipient) lost it, so I wanted to buy it back, thinking he would sell it cheaply, so I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: “Do not buy it, and do not consider it part of your original charity (i.e., do not retrieve it as if your donation is still valid), even if he gives it to you for a dirham, for one who returns to his charity is like one who returns to his vomit.” (Agreed upon) His saying: “I was carried on a horse for the sake of Allah” means: I gave it in charity to some of the Mujahideen."
"1614","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Avoid the seven calamities.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are they? He said: “Associating others with Allah, sorcery, and killing a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, consuming usury, devouring an orphan’s wealth, turning away on the day of battle, and slandering chaste, believing, heedless women” ((Agreed) On him, “the calamities” (the destructive ones).."
"1615","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who consumes usury and the one who pays it” [Muslim]. Al-Tirmidhi and others added [to the narration that the curse is also upon] his two witnesses and his scribe."
"1616","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Almighty Allah says"","" 'I am the One Who is most free from want of partners. He who does an action"","" associating others with Me besides Me"","" I will leave him and his associate (the one he associated with Me)..\"" [Muslim] .""
"1617","And on his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The first people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection is a man who was martyred. He was brought to him, and he recognized his blessing. He recognized it. He said: What did you do in it? He said: I fought for you until I was martyred. He said: You lied, but you fought so that it would be said: bold. It was said, and then he was ordered, so he was dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire. And a man who learned knowledge and taught it, and read the Qur’an, and it was brought to him, and he made known to him his blessings and he recognized them. He said, “What did you do in it?” He said, “I learned knowledge and taught it and I recited the Qur’an for Your sake.” He said, “You lied, but you learned so that it would be said: a scholar.” And you recited the Qur’an so that it would be said: “He is a reciter.” It was said: Then he was commanded to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire, and a man whom Allah expanded and gave him of various kinds. Money, so he brought it and he recognized his blessings, so he recognized them. He said: So what did you do in it? He said: I did not leave a path in which you like to be spent without spending in it for yourself. He said: You lied, but you did so that it would be said: Jawad, as it was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face and then thrown into the Fire” [Muslim]. (Footnote: Juri' (the word for 'bold') is pronounced with opening of the letter jim, breaking of the letter ra, and with elongation (madd), meaning: brave and competent.)"
"1618","Some people told me, We visit our rulers and we tell them things contrary to those which we say when we depart from them.\"" `Abdullah bin `Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) replied: \""In the era of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we considered this to be an act of hypocrisy.\"" [Al-Bukhari] .""
"1619","On the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah bin Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever shows off (his deeds for people), Allah will expose him (on the Day of Resurrection), and whoever shows off (his deeds to be glorified by people), Allah will expose his inner secrets to all of creation.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [It was also narrated by Muslim from the narration of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him]. “Heard” with emphasis on the meem, Its meaning is: He showed his work to people hypocrisy, “Allah heard about it,” that is, he will expose it on the Day of Resurrection, and the meaning is: “He who showed off,” meaning: He who showed people good deeds so that they might be glorified in their eyes, “Allah saw about him,” meaning: He showed his secret to the heads of creatures."
"1620","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever learns knowledge, seeking by it the face of Allah Almighty, but does not learn it except to gain a worldly benefit from it, will not smell the scent of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection,” meaning its scent. It was narrated by Abu Dawud with an authentic chain of transmission, and the hadiths on the subject are many and well-known."
"1621","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: What is your view about a man who does a righteous deed and people praise him for it?\"" He replied"","" \""This is the glad tidings which a believer receives (in this life).\"" [Muslim] .""
"1622","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The son of Adam is destined for his share of adultery, and he inevitably realizes that: the eyes are fornicated by looking, and the ears are fornicated by listening, and the tongue is the fornication of speaking, and the hand is the fornication of touching, and the foot is the fornication of stepping, and the heart desires and wishes, and the private part believes it or disbelieves it.” (Agreed upon. This is the wording of Muslim, and Al-Bukhari’s narration is brief.)"
"1623","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Avoid sitting on roadsides.\"" His Companions said: \""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) there is no other alternative but to sit there to talk.\"" Thereupon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""If you have to sit at all"","" then fulfill the rights of the road.\"" They asked: \""What are their rights?\"" Thereupon he said"","" \""Lowering the gaze (so that you may not stare at unlawful things); refraining from doing some harm to others"","" responding to greeting (i.e."","" saying 'Wa'alaikumus- salam' to one another) and commanding the good and forbidding the evil.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1624","On the authority of Abu Talha Zaid bin Sahl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were sitting in the courtyards talking in them, when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came and spoke to us and said: “What do you have to do with sitting on the pathways?” So we said: We only sat for nothing wrong with it. We sat discussing and talking. He said: “But no, then do what is right for you: lowering your gaze, returning your greetings, and being kind.” This term refers to pathways, as the word is formed with the letters"
"1625","On the authority of Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about sudden sight, and he said: “Avert your gaze” [Muslim]."
"1626","And on the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he was with Maimunah, when Ibn Umm Maktum came, and that was after we had been commanded to hijab. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Hide yourselves from him.” So we said: O Messenger of Allah, is he not blind? He does not see us nor recognize us. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Are you two blind?” Do you not see him?!” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1627","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, A man must not look at a man's private parts nor must a woman look at a woman's private parts; nor should a man be alone with a man under one cover"","" nor should a woman be alone with a woman under the same cover.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1628","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Avoid (entering a place) in which are women (uncovered or simply to mix with them in seclusion).\"" A man from the Ansar said"","" \""Tell me about the brother of a woman's husband.\"" He replied"","" \""The brother of a woman's husband is death.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1629","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should be alone with a woman except with a mahram” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1630","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, The sanctity of the wives of Mujahidun (i.e."","" those who strive hard and fight in the way of Allah) for those who remain at home (i.e."","" those who do not go to the battlefield to fight Jihad) is like the sanctity of their own mothers. Anyone who remains behind to look after the family of a Mujahid and betrays his trust"","" will be made to stand on the Day of Resurrection before the Mujahid who will take away from his meritorious deeds whatever he likes till he is satisfied.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned toward us and said"","" \""Now"","" what do you think (i.e."","" will he leave anything with him)?\"" [Muslim] .""
"1631","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men. And in a narration: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed men who imitate women, and women who imitate men. [Al-Bukhari]."
"1632","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the man who wears women’s clothing, and the woman who wears men’s clothing. [Abu Dawud]."
"1633","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two types of people of Hell that I have not seen: people who have whips like the tails of cows with which they beat people, and women who are clothed and naked, leaning forward, with their heads like the humps of a camel leaning forward. They will not enter Paradise, nor will they smell its scent, and its scent can be smelled from such-and-such a distance.” (Narrated by Muslim). The meaning of 'clothed' is from Allah’s blessings, and 'naked' refers to their ingratitude regarding them. It was said that its meaning is: She covers some of her body, and reveals some of it to show off her condition and the like. It was said: Its meaning is that she wears a thin garment that describes the color of her body. As for (maylat), it was said: It refers to obedience to Allah and what they are obliged to preserve. (Inclining) meaning they teach others their reprehensible actions, and it was said: They walk inclining, strutting, leaning their shoulders. It was said: Slanted women comb the slanted comb, which is the comb of prostitutes. Women tend to comb others with that comb. The meaning of “their heads are like the humps of a camel” is that they enlarge and magnify them by wrapping a turban or headband or the like."
"1634","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying: Do not eat with your left hand"","" because Satan eats and drinks with his left hand.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1635","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah said: “None of you should eat with his left hand, nor drink with it. Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with it” [Muslim]."
"1636","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying: Jews and Christians do not dye their hair"","" so act differently from them.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1637","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Quhafa, the father of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both, was brought on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and his head and beard were as white as the front teeth, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Change this and avoid blackness” [Muslim]."
"1638","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade shaving a part of the head. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"1639","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a boy, some portion of whose head was shaved and some of it was left out. He prohibited them from that and said, Shave the whole of it or leave the whole of it.\"" [Abu Dawud] .""
"1640","On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the family of Jaafar, may Allah be pleased with him, three days, then he came to them and said: “Do not cry for my brother after today.” Then he said: “Call for me my brother’s sons.” He brought us as if we were chicks and said: “Call for me the barber,” so he ordered him, and he shaved our heads.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1641","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited a woman from shaving her head. [An- Nasa'i] ."
"1642","A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have a daughter who had an attack of measles and her hair fell off. I have married her off; may I extend her hair (with extensions) for her?\"" Thereupon the Prophet (ﷺ) said"","" \""Allah has cursed the one who does hair extensions and the one who gets hair extensions.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1643","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, something similar, agreed upon."
"1644","And on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman that he heard Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, in the year he performed Hajj on the pulpit and he took up a lock of hair that was in the hands of a guard and said: O people of Medina, where is Your scholars? I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) forbidding such things and saying: “The Children of Israel were destroyed when they took these as their wives.” Agreed upon."
"1645","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the woman who does hair extensions, the woman who gets hair extensions, the tattooist, and the tattooed woman (Agreed upon)."
"1646","Allah has cursed those women who practise tattooing and those women who have themselves tattooed, and those women who order their eyebrows to be plucked for beauty, and those who make artificial spaces between their teeth for beauty, whereby they change Allah's creation. A woman started to argue with him, saying: What is all this?\"" He replied: \""Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed and who are cursed in Allah's Book? Allah"","" the Exalted"","" has said in His Book: \""And whatsoever the Messenger (Muhammad (ﷺ)) gives you"","" take it; and whatsoever he forbids you"","" abstain (from it).\"" (59:7) [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1647","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, He who does something contrary to our way (i.e."","" Islam) will have it rejected.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1648","On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “If one of you urinates, his penis should not be taken with his right hand, nor should he clean himself with his right hand, nor should he breathe in a vessel” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] and there are many authentic hadiths on this subject."
"1649","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should walk in one shoe in order to wear both of them or to take them all off.” And in a narration, “or to put on both of them together” (Agreed upon)."
"1650","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “If the strap of one of your sandals is cut, he should not walk on the other until he repairs it” [Muslim]."
"1651","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade a man to put on shoes while standing. [Abu Dawud]"
"1652","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Do not leave fire in your homes while you sleep” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1653","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A house in Medina burned down, affecting its people at night, and when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was informed about them, he said: “This fire is an enemy to you, so when you sleep, extinguish it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1654","And on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Cover the vessel, tie the waterskin, close the doors, and extinguish the lamp, for Satan does not loosen a waterskin, nor open a door, nor uncover a vessel. If any of you has no choice but to offer a stick over his vessel and mention the name of Allah, then let him do it, for the mouse (fuwaisiqa) sets fire to the house of the household.” [Muslim]) “Al-Fawisaqa” means a mouse, and “taḍarram” (the verb"
"1655","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: “We were forbidden from affectation (unnecessary pretense and formalities).” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1656","We visited 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with him) and he said to us: O people! He who has the knowledge of any matter may convey it to the others. And he who has no knowledge, thereof, should say: Allahu a'lam (Allah knows better).\"" It is a part and parcel of knowledge that a man who has no knowledge of a matter should say: \""Allah knows better.\"" Allah said to His Prophet (ﷺ): \""Say (O Muhammad (ﷺ)): 'No wage do I ask of you for this (the Qur'an)"","" nor am I one of the Mutakallifun (those who pretend and fabricate things which do not exist).\""' (38:86) [Al-Bukhari] .""
"1657","On the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The dead person is tortured in his grave for the wailing that was done over him.” And in a narration: “What was wailed over him” (Agreed upon)."
"1658","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who hits the cheeks, rips the pockets, and invokes with the invocation of the pre-Islamic era is not one of us” (Agreed upon)."
"1659","On the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: Abu Musa became ill and fainted, while his head was in the lap of a woman from his family. She came crying out loud, but he was unable to respond to her. When he woke up, he said: I am innocent of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was acquitted of. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is innocent of the woman who wails loudly (saaliqa), the woman who shaves her head (haalika), and the woman who tears her clothes (shaaqqa). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] “Al-Saliqa”: the one who raises her voice in lamentation and lamentation. Al-Halika: the one who shaves her head in the event of a severe calamity."
"1660","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, The one for whom wailing is performed (i.e."","" the deceased for whom people wail)"","" will be punished for it on the Day of Resurrection.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1661","On the authority of Umm Attiya Nusaybah - with the ḍammah of the nūn and its fatḥah - may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) enjoined upon us upon the pledge of allegiance that we should not mourn. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1662","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abdullah bin Rawahah, may Allah be pleased with him, fainted, and his sister started crying and saying: They made him, and so-and-so and so-and-so. she repeated her lament over him and said when he woke up: I did not say anything, but I was told: Are you like that?! [Al-Bukhari]."
"1663","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited Sa'd bin 'Ubadah during his illness. He was accompanied by 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Auf, Sa'd bin Abu Waqqas and 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with them). When they entered his house, they found him unconscious. The Messenger of Allah asked, Has he died?\"" They replied: \""No"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" Hearing this the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began to weep. When his Companions saw this"","" they also began to weep too. He said"","" \""Listen attentively: Allah does not punish for the shedding of tears or the grief of the heart"","" but takes to task or show mercy because of the utterances of this (and he pointed to his tongue).\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1664","On the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a woman wailing does not repent before her death, she will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a shield of scabs” [Muslim]."
"1665","On the authority of Usayd ibn Abi Usayd al-Tabi’i, on the authority of a woman who pledged allegiance, she said: “What the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) enjoined upon us was that we should not disobey him in the good deeds that he enjoined upon us: not to scratch our faces, not to pray for woe, not to tear the collar of our garments, and not to spread our hair.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1666","And on the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no dead person who dies, and he stands up and weeps, and says: ‘I brought him down, and his masters,’ or something like that, except that two angels would shake him and say, ‘Is that how you were?!’” [Al-Tirmidhi] ‘Al-haz’ refers to pushing with the palm of the hand in the chest."
"1667","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two things in people that cause disbelief: slandering one’s lineage, and wailing over the dead” [Muslim]."
"1668","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked people about soothsayers, and he said: “They are nothing.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, they sometimes tell us something, so is it true? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “That word of truth is snatched by the genie. He reads it into the ear of his guardian, and they mix with it a hundred lies.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Al-Bukhari on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The angels descend in the clouds - which are the clouds - so remember the matter has been decided in the sky, so Satan eavesdrops, hears it, and suggests it to the soothsayers, and they tell a hundred lies of their own accord with it.” His saying: “So he says it” is by opening the yā and combining the qāf and the ra’, meaning: he throws it, and “al-‘anan” is by opening the ain."
"1669","Narrated Safiyyah, daughter of Abu 'Ubaid, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said, He who goes to one who claims to tell about matters of the Unseen and believes in him"","" his Salat (prayers) will not be accepted for forty days.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1670","And on the authority of Qabisa bin Al-Mukhariq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Al-Ayyafah, Al-Tira, and Al-Tariq are from the Jabbat.” [Abu Dawud]. He said: ‘Al-Tariq’ refers to divination by bird flight: that is, a person takes a good omen if the bird flies to the right, and a bad omen if it flies to the left. Abu Dawud said: “And Al-Ayyafah”: the calligraphy. Al-Jawhari said in Al-Sihah: Jibt is a word used to refer to an idol, a priest, a magician, and the like."
"1671","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever acquires knowledge from the stars, acquires a branch of magic, more will be added.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1672","On the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I am a recent covenant of ignorance, and Allah Almighty brought Islam, and that among us are men who go to soothsayers? He said: “So do not go to them.” I said: And among us are men who take omens? He said: “That is something they find in their chests, so it does not deter them.” I said: And among us are men who draw lines (for omens)? He said: “A prophet among the prophets used to write handwriting, so whoever agreed with his handwriting, that is it.” [Muslim]."
"1673","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the money given to a soothsayer. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"1674","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Not the transmission of disease of one person to another and no evil omen"","" but I am pleased with good omens.\"" He was asked: \""What is good omen?\"" He replied"","" \""A good word.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1675","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, There is no infection and no evil omen; but if there is anything (that may be a source of trouble) then it could be a house"","" a horse"","" and a woman.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1676","On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not practice omens. [Abu Dawud]"
"1677","When talking of omens was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said, The best type of omen is the good omen.\"" He added"","" \""A Muslim should not refrain from anything because of an omen.\"" He (ﷺ) told them"","" \""When any of you sees anything which he dislikes"","" he should say: 'Allahuma la ya'ti bil-hasanati illa Anta"","" wa la yadfa'us- sayyi'ati illa Anta"","" wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa Bika (O Allah ! You Alone bring good things; You Alone avert evil things"","" and there is no might or power but in You).\""' [Abu Dawud with Sahih Isnad] .""
"1678","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Those who make these images will be tortured on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1679","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came from a journey, and I had covered up a shelf of mine with a curtain in which there were statues. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw it, his face changed and he said: “O Aisha, the people most tormented by Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who are compared to Allah’s creation.” She said: So we cut it off and made one or two pillows out of it. ((Agreed) On him). “Al-Sahwah” with the opening of the neglected sīn, which is: the sāfah is between the two sides of the house, and it was said: it is the strand that penetrates the wall."
"1680","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, Every painter will go to Hell"","" and for every portrait he has made"","" there will be appointed one who will chastise him in the Hell.\"" Ibn 'Abbas said: If you have to do it"","" draw pictures of trees and other inanimate things. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1681","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever makes pictures in this world, will be required to breathe the soul into them on the Day of Resurrection, but he will not be able to blow them.” (Agreed upon)"
"1682","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The people who will be most severely tormented on the Day of Resurrection are those who make pictures” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1683","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, The Almighty Allah said: 'Who is more an oppressor than him who goes to create like My creation? Let him make a particle"","" a grain"","" or a grain of barley.\""' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1684","On the authority of Abu Talha, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1685","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) promised Gabriel that he would come to him, but he was delayed until it became difficult for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So he went out, met Gabriel, and complained to him, whereupon Gabriel said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image. [Al-Bukhari] ((“Rath”: slower, and it is with a thā’). triangle).."
"1686","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) promised Jibril (Gabriel) that he would come at a definite hour; that hour came but he did not come to him. There was a staff in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He threw it from his hand and said, Never does Allah back out of His Promise"","" nor do His messengers.\"" Then he noticed a puppy under his bed and said"","" \""O 'Aishah"","" when did this dog enter?\"" She said: \""By Allah"","" I don't know.\"" He then commanded that it should be turned out. No sooner than had they expelled it"","" Jibril came and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him"","" \""You promised to visit me. I waited for you but you did not come.\"" Whereupon he said: \""The dog kept me from coming. We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1687","On the authority of Abu Al-Hayyaj Hayyan bin Husayn, he said: Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: Shall I not send you to do what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to do? That you do not leave an image without obliterating it, and no elevated grave without leveling it. [Muslim]."
"1688","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, He who keeps a dog other than one for hunting or herding"","" will lose two Qirat every day out of his rewards.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1689","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat of his work will be deducted every day from his work, except for a plowing or livestock dog” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: “Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog nor a land dog, two qirats will be deducted from his reward for each day."
"1690","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Angels do not accompany a traveling party that has a dog or a bell with it.” [Muslim]"
"1691","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The bell is one of the musical instruments of Satan.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1692","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade riding the Jallalah (a specific type of camel considered impure) among the camels. [Abu Dawud]"
"1693","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. What is meant is burying it if the mosque is dirt or sand and the like. So he buries it under the dirt of the mosque. Abu Al-Mahasin Al-Ruwani, one of our companions, said in his book (Al-Bahr), and it was said: What is meant by burying her is to remove her from the mosque, but if the mosque is tiled or plastered, he rubs it on the mosque floor with his shoe or something else, as many ignorant people do. This is not a burial, but rather an increase in sin and an increase of filth in the mosque. The mosque, and whoever does that must wipe it after that with his clothes, hand, or something else, or wash it."
"1694","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw mucous, saliva, or phlegm on the wall of the qibla and scratched it [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1695","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “These mosques are not suitable for any urine or filth. Rather, they are for the remembrance of Allah Almighty and the reading of the Qur’an.” Or as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said [Muslim]."
"1696","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever hears a man seeking a lost item in the mosque should say: May Allah not return her to you, for mosques were not built for this” [Muslim]."
"1697","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, say: May Allah not make you profit from your trade, and if you see someone seeking a lost item, say: May Allah not return it to you.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1698","A man announced (the loss of his camel) in the mosque, uttering these words: Has any one seen my red camel?\"" Upon this the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""You did not find it here"","" for mosques were not built for this.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1699","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade buying and selling in the mosque, or for a lost item to be sought there, or for poetry to be recited there. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1700","While I was in the mosque, someone threw a pebble at me, and when I looked up, I saw that it was 'Umar bin Al-Khattab, who said: Go and call me these two men.\"" I brought them and 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with him) asked them: \""Where are you from?\"" On their replying that they belonged to At-Taif"","" he said: \""Had you been the inhabitants of Al-Madinah"","" I would have given you a beating for raising your voices in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" [Al- Bukhari] .""
"1701","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who has eaten garlic should not come to our mosque.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] . The narration in Muslim is: \""He who has eaten garlic should not come to our mosques.\""
"1702","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who has eaten from this plant (i.e."","" garlic) should not approach us and should not offer Salat (prayer) along with us.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1703","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever eats garlic or onions should isolate himself from us, or should isolate himself from our mosque” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: “Whoever eats onions, garlic, or leeks, should not come near our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what our sons are harmed by.” Adam."
"1704","On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he preached on Friday and said in his sermon: Then you people eat two trees that I see as nothing but evil: onions and garlic - I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he found their scent coming from a man in the mosque, he ordered him to go out to Al-Baqi’, and whoever eats them, let him cook them thoroughly. [Muslim]."
"1705","On the authority of Moaz bin Anas Al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade sitting alone on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1706","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Whoever has a sacrificial animal to sacrifice"","" when the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah is sighted"","" should not cut his hair or trim his nails until he has offered his sacrifice.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1707","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty forbids you from swearing by your fathers, so whoever swears, let him swear by Allah, or keep silent.” (Agreed upon). And in a narration in the Sahih, “So whoever swears, let him swear by Allah, or keep silent.”"
"1708","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not swear by idols, nor by your fathers.” [Muslim]. “Taghut”: the plural of Taghut, which refers to idols, and from it is the hadith: “This is the Taghut of Daws.” “Daws”: meaning: their idol and their deity, and it is narrated in other hadith collections: “By the Taghut” is the plural of Taghut, which is Satan and the idol."
"1709","On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever swears to be honest is not one of us.” [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with an authentic chain of transmission]"
"1710","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, If anyone swears that in such and such case he will be free from Islam and afterwards he turns out to be a liar"","" he will be as he has sworn; but if he is speaking the truth"","" he will not revert safely to Islam.\"" [Abu Dawud] .""
"1711","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he heard a man say: No, by the Kaaba. Ibn Omar said: Do not swear by anything other than Allah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever swears by other than Allah has disbelieved or committed polytheism.” [Al-Tirmidhi] Some scholars interpreted his saying: “He has disbelieved or committed polytheism” as saying: Exaggeration, as it was narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Hypocrisy is shirk.”"
"1712","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever wrongfully seizes the wealth of a Muslim without right, will meet Allah while He is angry with him.” He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) read to us an authentication from the Book of Allah Almighty: {Indeed, those who buy the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price} [Al Imran: 77] until the end of the verse: [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1713","And on the authority of Abu Umamah Iyas bin Tha’labah Al-Harithi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever takes away the right of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has made Hell obligatory for him - and forbidden Paradise for him.” A man said to him: Even if it is a small thing, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Even if it is a twig of arāk (a small stick from the arāk tree)” ([Muslim].."
"1714","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The major sins: associating partners with Allah, disobeying one’s parents, murder (of an innocent person), and swearing a false oath” [Al-Bukhari]. And in a narration: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins? He said: Associating others with Allah. He said: Then what? He said: the oath that leads one to ruin (i.e., a false oath taken to wrongfully seize another's wealth). I said: What is a dimpled oath? He said: He who wrongfully seizes the wealth of a Muslim means an oath in which he is a liar."
"1715","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, When you take an oath and consider something else to be better than it"","" make expiation for your oath and choose the better alternative.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1716","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever takes an oath and sees something else better than it, let him expiate his oath and do what is better” [Muslim]."
"1717","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Verily"","" I swear by Allah"","" if Allah wills"","" I shall not swear to do something but that if I consider something else to be better than it"","" then I shall make expiation for my oath and adopt the thing that is better.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1718","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “For one of you to persist in his oath is more sinful before Allah Almighty than to give the expiation that Allah has imposed upon him.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] His saying: “to enter” with the opening of the lam and the emphasis on the jim: that is, he goes too far in it, And he does not disbelieve. His saying: “sinful” is with the triple tha’, meaning: more sinful."
"1719","The Ayah: Allah will not punish you for what is unintentional in your oaths ...\"" was revealed in respect of those persons who are in the habit of repeating: 'No"","" by Allah'; and 'Yes"","" by Allah.' [Al- Bukhari] .""
"1720","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Swearing is a waste of goods and a loss of gain” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1721","On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Beware of swearing too much in sales, for he spends and then loses” [Muslim]."
"1722","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No one asks (for anything) by the countenance of Allah except Paradise” [Abu Dawud]."
"1723","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever seeks refuge in Allah, grant him refuge, and whoever asks Allah, give him, and whoever calls you, answer him, and whoever does you a favor, reward him. If you do not find something to reward him with, then pray for him until you see that you have rewarded him.” ((An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud and Al-Nasa’i.) With the chain of transmission of the two Sahihs.)"
"1724","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The most despicable name in the sight of Allah Almighty is a man called the King of Kings” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Sufyan bin Uyaynah said: “The King of Kings” is an example of: Shaheen Shah."
"1725","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Do not address a hypocrite with the title of chief"","" (or similar titles of respect) for even if he deserves this title you will invite Allah's Wrath by using it for him.\"" [Abu Dawud] .""
"1726","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon Umm al-Sa’ib, or Umm al-Musayyab, and said: “Why are you trembling, Umm al-Sa’ib - or Umm al-Musayyab?” She said: “Fever, may Allah not bless it.” He said: “Do not curse fever, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam, just as furnace removes the impurities from iron.” [Muslim]). “You tremble,” meaning you move quickly, and its meaning is: you tremble. It is with the ḍammah of the ta’, with the repeated zay and the repeated fa’, and it was also narrated with the repeated ra’ and the qāfīn."
"1727","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Do not revile the wind. When you experience something abominable (about it)"","" supplicate: 'Allahumma inna nas'aluka min khairi hadhihir-rihi"","" wa khairi ma fiha"","" wa khairi ma umirat bihi. Wa na'udhu bika min sharri hadhihir-rihi"","" wa sharri ma fiha"","" wa sharri ma umirat bihi. (O Allah"","" we beg of You the good of this wind and the good of that which it contains and the good of that which it has been commanded; and we seek refuge in you from the evil of this wind and the evil of that which it contains and the evil of that which it has been commanded).\"" [At-Tirmidhi] .""
"1728","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The wind is from the Spirit of Allah. It brings mercy and it brings torment, so if you see it, do not curse it, and ask Allah for its goodness, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil.” [Abu Dawud] His saying (ﷺ) from the Spirit of Allah is with the opening of the rā’, meaning His mercy toward His servants"
"1729","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the wind blew, the Prophet (ﷺ) would say: “O Allah, I ask You for its good, and the good of what is in it, and the good of what it was sent with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what it was sent with” [Muslim]."
"1730","On the authority of Zaid bin Khadel Al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not curse the rooster, for it wakes you up for prayer.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1731","On the authority of Zaid bin Khalid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in the morning prayer in Al-Hudaybiyyah in the wake of night rain. When he finished, he approached the people and said: “Do you know what your Lord said?” They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He said: “Among my servants has become a believer in me and a disbeliever in me. He said: “We have been rained upon by the grace and mercy of Allah,” and that one is a believer in Me who disbelieves in the stars. As for whoever says, “We have rained under such-and-such a storm,” that is a disbeliever in Me who believes in the stars.” (Agreed upon) And the sky here: rain."
"1732","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a man says to his brother: O infidel, then one of them has fulfilled it. If it is as he said, otherwise it returns upon him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1733","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever calls a man a disbeliever, or says: The enemy of Allah, and he is not like that except that it returns upon him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Hot will return."
"1734","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, A true believer does not taunt or curse or abuse or talk indecently.\"" [At-Tirmidhi] .""
"1735","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Indecency does not leave anything untainted and decency does not leave anything ungraced and embellished.\"" [At- Tirmidhi] .""
"1736","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Those who exaggerate are destroyed.” He said it three times. [Narrated by Muslim. “Those who exaggerate”: those who exaggerate in matters]."
"1737","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Verily"","" Allah dislikes an eloquent person who rolls his tongue as a cow rolls its tongue (while eating).\"" [Abu Dawud and At- Tirmidhi] .""
"1738","On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The one who loves me the most and is the closest to me in assembly on the Day of Resurrection will have the best morals among you, and the one who hates you the most to me and the farthest from me on the Day of Resurrection are the chatterers, the rants, and the talkative ones.” [Al-Tirmidhi]. It was previously explained in Chapter on good manners..."
"1739","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has been filthy,’ but let him say, ‘I have filthed myself.’” (Agreed upon)). The scholars said the meaning of filth is that is, “I vomited,” which is the meaning of “I have filthed,” but the word filth is disliked."
"1740","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not call grapes al-Karm, for al-Karm is the Muslim” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. [And this is a Muslim wording]. And in a narration: “For generosity is only the heart of the believer.” And in a narration by Al-Bukhari. And Muslim: “They say generosity, but generosity is the heart of the believer.”"
"1741","On the authority of Wael bin Hajar, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Do not say: the vineyard, but say: the grape, and the habala.” It was narrated by Muslim al-Habla by opening the ha and the ba, and it is also said by placing the ba in the suffix."
"1742","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A woman should not look at another woman, so that she describes her to her husband as if he were looking at her” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1743","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, You must not supplicate: 'O Allah! forgive me if You wish; O Allah bestow mercy on me if You wish.' But beg from Allah with certitude for no one has the power to compel Allah.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] Another narration of Muslim is: \""A supplication should be made in full confidence and one should persistently express his desire (before Allah) in his supplication"","" for no bounty is too great for Allah to bestow (upon his slaves).\""
"1744","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, When one of you supplicates"","" let him be decisive and he should not say: 'O Allah"","" bestow upon me such and such if You wish'"","" because no one has the power to compel Him.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1745","On the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Do not say: What Allah willed and so-and-so willed, but say: What Allah willed, then so-and-so willed.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1746","On the authority of Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) disliked sleeping before the Isha prayer and talking after it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1747","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed the evening prayer at the end of his life, and when he said the salutation, he said: “Have you seen this night of yours? For when a hundred years have passed, not a single person of those living on the earth today will remain” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1748","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that they waited for the Prophet (ﷺ) and he came to them near the middle of the night and led them in the evening prayer. He said: Then he addressed us and said: “But the people have prayed. Then they fell asleep, and you will not stop praying as long as you wait for the prayer” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1749","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, If a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses"","" and thus he spends the night angry with her"","" the angels continue cursing her till the morning.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1750","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not permissible for a woman to fast while her husband is present except with his permission, and she should not give permission to anyone in his house except with his permission” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1751","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Does not one of you fear that if he raises his head before the imam, Allah will make his head the head of a donkey! Or Allah will make his image the image of a donkey?” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1752","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade placing hands on the waist during prayer. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1753","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - (ﷺ) - saying: “There is no prayer in the presence of food, nor while one is in need of relieving himself from the two impure substances (urine and feces).” [Muslim]."
"1754","On the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: “What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer?” Then his words about that became more severe until he said: “Let them refrain from that, or their sight will be snatched away”! . [Al-Bukhari]"
"1755","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about turning around during prayer, and he said: “It is a theft that Satan steals from a servant’s prayer” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1756","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “Beware of turning around during prayer, for turning around during prayer is fatal. If it is unavoidable, then it is permissible in voluntary prayer, not in obligatory prayer.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1757","On the authority of Abu Marthad Kinaz bin Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Do not pray at (or on) graves, and do not sit on them” [Muslim]."
"1758","On the authority of Abu Al-Juhaim Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Al-Samah Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If the one passing between the one praying knew what is incumbent upon him (i.e., the sin he would incur), it would be better for him to stop for forty than to pass in front of him.” [The narrator said: I don’t know if he said forty days, or forty months, or forty years]. (Agreed On him).."
"1759","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “If the prayer is established, then there is no prayer except the obligatory prayer” [Muslim]."
"1760","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Do not choose the Friday night among all other nights for standing in (Tahajjud) prayer"","" and do not choose Friday among all other days for Saum (fasting) except that it is part of a fast that one of you is observing.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1761","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “None of you should fast on Friday except the day before or after it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1762","On the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, he said: I asked Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: Did the Prophet (ﷺ) forbid fasting on Friday? He said: Yes [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1763","Juwairiyah bint Al-Harith (May Allah be pleased with her), the Mother of the Believers, said that the Prophet (ﷺ) visited her on a Friday and she was observing fast. He asked, Did you observe fast yesterday?\"" She said"","" \""No.\"" He asked"","" \""Do you intend to observe fast tomorrow?\"" She said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""In that case"","" give up your fast today.\"" [Al-Bukhari] .""
"1764","On the authority of Abu Hurairah and Aisha, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade continuous fasting (al-wasal). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1765","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited observing continuous fasts beyond one day. The Companions submitted: But you do it.\"" He replied"","" \""I am not like you. I am given to eat and to drink (from Allah).\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1766","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you sits on an ember and his clothes are burned and removed from his skin, it is better for him than for him to sit on a grave” [Muslim]"
"1767","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade plastering the grave, sitting on it, or building on it. [Muslim]"
"1768","On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Any slave who runs away absolves his owner of responsibility for him.” [Muslim]"
"1769","And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ): “If a slave runs away, his prayer will not be accepted.” [Muslim]. And in a narration: “He has disbelieved.”"
"1770","And on the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Quraysh were concerned about the matter of the Makhzoumiya woman who had stolen, so they said: Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about it? They said: Who would dare to speak to him (to intercede with him) except Usamah bin Zayd, whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) loved? Then Osama spoke to him and he (ﷺ) said: “Do you intercede regarding one of the limits set by Allah Almighty?” Then he stood up and delivered a sermon. Then he said: “The destruction of those before you was that if the noble among them stole, they would abandon him, and if the weak among them stole, they would impose punishment on him, and by Allah, if Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, had stolen, I would have cut off her hand.” (Agreed upon)). And in a narration, the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) colored, so he said: “Do you intercede in one of Allah’s punishments?” He said. Osama: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then he ordered that woman to have her hand cut off"
"1771","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Beware of those who relieve themselves in public pathways and shade.” They said: What is the curser? He said: “The one who abandons people’s path or in their shade” [Muslim]."
"1772","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade urinating in stagnant water. [Muslim]"
"1773","On the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a father of his was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “I have gifted this son of mine a slave who was mine.” the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Did you give your other sons a gift like this?” He said: “No.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Send him back.” And in a narration: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: He said: “Did you do this to all of your children?” He said: “No.” He said: “Fear Allah and be just among your children.” So my father came back and returned that charity. And in a narration: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Bashir, do you have a son other than this one?” He said: Yes. He said: “No, I did not give them such a gift.” “This?” He said: No. He said: “Then do not bear witness to me, for I do not bear witness to injustice.” And in one narration: “Do not bear witness to me against injustice.” In another narration: “Someone else bears witness to this.” Then he said: “Would you be pleased that they should be equal to you in righteousness?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then no.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1774","On the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, may Allah be pleased with them both, she said: She went to see Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with him, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) when her father, Abu Sufyan bin Harb, may Allah be pleased with him, died. She called for perfume that contained yellowish-purple or something else, and she anointed a slave girl with it, then touched her cheeks. Then she said: By Allah, I have no need for perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say on the pulpit: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a dead person for more than three nights, except for a husband for four months and ten days.” Zainab said: Then she went to Zainab bint Jahsh, may Allah be pleased with her, when her brother died, so she asked for perfume, so she touched it, then she said: By Allah, I have no need for perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying on the pulpit: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day.” To mourn a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband, is four months and ten days” (Agreed upon)."
"1775","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that a person in the city should make a deal on behalf of a villager on commission even if he is his real brother.\ [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]""
"1776","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, Do not meet the merchandise till they arrive in the market.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1777","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not meet [caravans of] riders to purchase their goods before they reach the market, and do not let a city dweller sell on behalf of a villager.” Tawus said to him: What is the meaning of his saying: No sale by a city dweller for a Bedouin? He said: He should not have a broker. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1778","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade a city dweller from selling on behalf of a villager, and forbade artificially raising prices through fake bidding (نجش). A man should not sell on the basis of his brother’s sale, nor should a man propose to a woman who is already engaged to his brother. A woman should not ask her husband to divorce her co-wife (sister) in order to take for herself what is in her sister's care (the husband's full provision and attention). In a narration, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade meeting trade caravans to buy goods before they reach the market, and forbade a migrant (to Madinah) from buying on behalf of a Bedouin, and forbade a woman from stipulating in her marriage contract that her co-wife (sister) be divorced, and forbade a man from outbidding his brother in an auction, and forbade fake bidding (نجش) and the practice of hiding defects in livestock (تصرية)” (Agreed upon)."
"1779","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not sell to one of you on the basis of selling to others, and do not propose an engagement after his brother proposes unless he gives him permission” [Agreed upon, and this is the Muslim wording]"
"1780","On the authority of Uqba bin Amer, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A believer is the brother of a believer, so it is not permissible for a believer to make a purchase on the basis of his brother’s sale or propose an engagement on the basis of his brother’s proposal until he abandons it” [Muslim]."
"1781","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty is pleased with three things for you, and He hates three things for you: He is pleased with you that you worship Him, and do not associate anything with Him, and that you hold fast to the rope of Allah all together and do not become divided. And He hates for you: gossip, asking too much, and wasting money” ([Muslim]. Explanation).."
"1782","Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah dictated a letter to me addressed to Mu'awiyah (May Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate at the end of each obligatory Salat (prescribed prayer): La ilaha illallahu"","" wahadahu la sharika lahu"","" lahul-mulku"","" wa lahul-hamdu"","" wa Huwa 'ala kulli shai'in Qadir. Allahumma la mani'a lima a'taita"","" wa la mu'tiya lima mana'ta"","" wa la yanfa'u dhal-jaddi mink-al-jaddu. (There is no true god except Allah"","" the One"","" Who has no partner. His is the sovereignty and His is the praise"","" and He is Able to do everything. O Allah! Nobody can withhold what You give; and nobody can give what You withhold; and the high status of a person is of no avail against Your Will).\"" He also wrote to him that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to forbid irrelevant talk"","" wasteful expenditure"","" persistent questioning"","" disobedience of parents (especially mothers)"","" infanticide of daughters by burying them alive"","" depriving others of their rights and acquisition of property wrongfully. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1783","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who said: “None of you should point a weapon at his brother, for he does not know, perhaps Satan will snatch it from his hand, and he will fall into a pit of fire.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim, he said: Abu Al-Qasim (ﷺ) said: “Whoever points at his brother with an iron, the angels will curse him, until he withdraws his weapon.” Even if he is his brother to his father and mother.” The Prophet’s (ﷺ) saying “yanza’” (ينزع) has two authentic recitations: one with the unmarked letter ع (عین مهملة) and زاي (zay) with kasra, the other with the dotted غ (غین معجمة) and زاي with fatha. Both meanings are similar: it means to throw/cast, and to corrupt/damage. The original meaning of"
"1784","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade handling a drawn sword.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"1785","We were sitting with Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) in the mosque when the Mu'adhdhin proclaimed the Adhan. A man stood up in the mosque and started walking out. Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) stared at him till he went out of the mosque. Upon this Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, this man has disobeyed Abul-Qasim (ﷺ). [Muslim] ."
"1786","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, He who is presented with a flower of sweet basil should not reject it"","" because it is light in weight and pleasant in odour.\"" [Muslim] .""
"1787","On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not reject perfume” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1788","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard a man praising a man and praising him, so he said: “You destroyed, or cut off the man’s back” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (23)."
"1789","On the authority of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man was mentioned to the Prophet (ﷺ) and a man praised him well, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Woe to you! You cut the neck of your companion.” He says it repeatedly, “And if one of you is inevitably praising, let him say: I think such-and-such if he sees that it is like that, and Allah will judge him, and no one may declare anyone pure before Allah.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1790","And on the authority of Hammam bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Miqdad, may Allah be pleased with him, when a man began praising Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him. So Al-Miqdad did so, and he knelt down and began to throw gravel in his face, and Uthman said to him: What is your business? He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If you see those praising them, throw dust in their faces.” [Muslim]). These hadiths prohibit, and there are many authentic hadiths regarding permissibility. The scholars said: The way to combine the hadiths is to say: If the one being praised has perfect faith, certainty, self-control, and complete knowledge such that he is not tempted, nor is he deceived by it, nor is he playing with it, then it is neither forbidden nor reprehensible, and if any of these matters are feared for him, he dislikes praising him to his face with extreme hatred, and this detail is revealed. The various hadiths on this matter. Among the permissibility is his saying (ﷺ) to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: “I hope that you will be one of them,” meaning one of those who are called upon from all gates of Paradise to enter it, and in the other hadith: “I am not one of them,” meaning: I am not one of those who let down their backs out of arrogance. And he (ﷺ) said to Omar, may Allah be pleased with him: “Satan has not seen you walking around rudely.” Except that he behaved in a rude way other than being rude.” There are many hadiths regarding permissibility, and a number of their aspects were mentioned in the book: “Al-Adhkar.”"
"1791","And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, went out to the Levant until when he was at Sarg, the commanders of the soldiers - Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah and his companions - met him and informed him that the epidemic had occurred in the Levant. Ibn Abbas said: Omar said: Call for me the first emigrants, so I called them, consulted them, and told them that the epidemic had occurred in the Levant, but they disagreed, and some of them said: you went out for a mission, and we do not think you should return from it. And some of them said: With you are the rest of the people and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we do not think you should advance them towards this epidemic. So he said: Get away from me, then he said: Call for me the Ansar. So I called them, so he consulted them, and they followed the path of the immigrants, and disagreed as they disagreed, so he said: Get away from me, then he said: Call for me whoever of the sheikhdom of Quraysh, from the emigrants of conquest, was here, so I called them, none of them disagreed with him (all agreed with him). They said: We think that you return with the people, and do not introduce them to this epidemic, so Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, called out to the people: I will set out in the morning, so they went in the morning, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Fleeing from the decree of Allah? So Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If there was someone other than you, he would say it, O Abu Ubaida! - and Omar hated to disagree with him - yes, fleeing from the decree of Allah to the decree of Allah. Have you seen if you had camels? So I descended into a valley with two flanks, one of which is fertile and the other is barren. Isn’t it that if I graze the fertile land, I graze it according to the power of Allah, and if I graze the barren land, then I graze it according to the power of Allah? And if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave [the land] fleeing from it.” Then Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, thanked Allah Almighty and left. (Agreed upon) Al-Adwa: the side of the valley."
"1792","On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If you hear of plague in a land, do not enter it, and if it occurs in a land and you are in it, do not leave it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1793","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Avoid the seven major [destructive] sins.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are they? He said: “Associating others with Allah, sorcery, killing a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, consuming usury, consuming an orphan’s wealth, turning away on the day of battle, and slandering chaste and unaware women” ((Agreed) On him).."
"1794","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: “the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade traveling with the Qur’an to enemy territory” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1795","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who drinks from vessels of silver only draws the fire of Hell into his stomach” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: “He who eats or drinks from vessels of silver and gold.”"
"1796","On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade us from using silk, brocade, and drinking from vessels of gold and silver, and he said: “They are for them in this world and they are yours in the hereafter” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration in the Two Sahihs on the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Do not wear silk or brocade, do not drink from vessels of gold and silver, and do not eat from their dishes [made of gold or silver].”"
"1797","I was with Anas bin Malik (May Allah be pleased with him) in the company of some Magians when Faludhaj (a sweet made of flour and honey) was brought in a silver utensil, and Anas did not take it. The man was told to change the utensil. So he changed the utensil and when he brought it to Anas, he took it. [Al-Baihaqi] ."
"1798","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade a man from saffron. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1799","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) saw two yellow garments and said: “Your mother ordered you to do this?” I said: Wash them? He said: “Rather, burn them.” And in a narration, he said: “This is one of the clothes of the infidels, so do not wear it” ([Muslim].."
"1800","On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): “No fasting should be completed after a wet dream, nor ritual silence from a day until the night.” Al-Khattabi said in the interpretation of this hadith: One of the rituals of pre-Islamic times was ritual silence ("
"1801","On the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon a woman from Ahmose called Zainab, and he saw that she was not speaking. He said: Why is she not speaking? They said: She is mute (unable to speak), so he said to her: Speak, for this is not permissible. This is the work of pre-Islamic times! So she spoke. [Al-Bukhari]"
"1802","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father and knows that he is not his father, then Paradise is forbidden to him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1803","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Do not turn away from your fathers"","" for he who turns away from his father"","" will be guilty of committing an act of disbelief.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]""
"1804","And on the authority of Yazid bin Sharik bin Tariq, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, on the pulpit giving a sermon, and I heard him say: No, by Allah, we do not have a book to read except the Book of Allah, and what is in this document. So he spread it, and found in it were camel teeth and things of wounds, and in it: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Medina is sacred from a caravan to a bull. The curse of Allah, the angels, and all of mankind is upon him. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any repentance or ransom. The covenant of the Muslims is one, and the lowest of them will strive to fulfill it. Whoever betrays a Muslim, then the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people will be upon him. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection any repentance or ransom. And whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or belongs to someone other than his patrons/allies, then the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people will be upon him. Allah will not accept it from him on the Day of Resurrection. The Resurrection is pure and not just.” (Agreed upon) Al-Sarf: repentance (or alternatively, means). Al-Adl: ransom/compensation."
"1805","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: A person who attributes his fatherhood to anyone other than his real father"","" knowing that he is not his father"","" commits an act of disbelief. And he who makes a claim of anything which in fact does not belong to him"","" is none of us. He should make his abode in Hell"","" and he who labels anyone as disbeliever or calls him the enemy of Allah and he is in fact not so"","" his charge will revert to him.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1806","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah"","" the Exalted"","" is jealous"","" and His jealousy is provoked when a person does what Allah has declared unlawful.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .""
"1807","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever swears an oath and says in his oath: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, let him say: There is no god but Allah, and whoever says to his companion: Allah Almighty, I will gamble with you, let him give alms” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
